        "slc_c6fbeab0d0b61bee901c82cc18864369e435ad1bc65e62f0107a334b4958ac46"
      ],
      "text": "The Agent Gateway is described as an agentic orchestration framework offering native support for Snowflake tools."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_37de4c1411acb67cefa0a66299b55fee0b2383dfbba4da1721f77c274c6d91d7",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9",
          "git_sha": "7690c2011390cd2896c39c5c113e52ead74ae9ff",
          "line_end": 8,
          "line_start": 6,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "snowflake-labs/orchestration-framework",
          "url": "https://github.com/Snowflake-Labs/orchestration-framework/blob/9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9/README.md#L6-L8"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_2e0d063c3034c143145c64abab9dc73d71f12843e71ef8e6701b7299715e7698"
      ],
      "text": "Rather than forcing users to choose between Cortex Search RAG and Cortex Analyst Text2SQL, the gateway routes each request to the appropriate tool."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_512ae7d1a9db19ca531a9bc83a7874c76b591647898c50904ad277d1aac525f5",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "interfaces",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9",
          "git_sha": "7690c2011390cd2896c39c5c113e52ead74ae9ff",
          "line_end": 17,
          "line_start": 10,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "snowflake-labs/orchestration-framework",
          "url": "https://github.com/Snowflake-Labs/orchestration-framework/blob/9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9/README.md#L10-L17"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_c57ec7029b3c81c0cb62861dd3498393dda299ff64a9da59c49c3145790d9158"
      ],
      "text": "The framework supports four tool types: Cortex Search for unstructured data, Cortex Analyst for structured data, Python for custom operations such as third-party API calls, and SQL for custom user-built SQL pipelines."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_6ac89ab9f6d3e38383bcec97331e611a132ecd376c975548764d78d8d12a99cb",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9",
          "git_sha": "7690c2011390cd2896c39c5c113e52ead74ae9ff",
          "line_end": 217,
          "line_start": 216,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "snowflake-labs/orchestration-framework",
          "url": "https://github.com/Snowflake-Labs/orchestration-framework/blob/9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9/README.md#L216-L217"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_10300aafc6f2327c0a7fc1753460136069f32bb6296ef0d38dfa2076e95651fe"
      ],
      "text": "A dedicated planner LLM decomposes the user's request into an execution plan, forming a task graph that invokes tool calls asynchronously and in parallel where possible, with Snowflake compute used for plan generation and tool execution."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_d46995aa72fa0ac1ad62f0e83cfbdc13c5d80c684e3b247f642edeb8a787bbde",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9",
          "git_sha": "7690c2011390cd2896c39c5c113e52ead74ae9ff",
          "line_end": 217,
          "line_start": 216,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "snowflake-labs/orchestration-framework",
          "url": "https://github.com/Snowflake-Labs/orchestration-framework/blob/9addb6d4b303a0bbbc25da1f26d017e8504131e9/README.md#L216-L217"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_10300aafc6f2327c0a7fc1753460136069f32bb6296ef0d38dfa2076e95651fe"
      ],
      "text": "The architecture is stated to leverage the LLM Compiler design from Berkeley AI Research Lab, citing a 2024 paper on parallel function calling."
    },
